{
  "id": "EUVD-2026-54507",
  "enisaUuid": "04ec95d1-0d04-3328-93fd-99d5e28ea0ac",
  "description": "A vulnerability in the GPT file format parser of ClamAV could allow an unauthenticated, remote attacker to cause a DoS condition or possibly other expanded impacts as a result of&nbsp;memory corruption on an affected device.\r\n\r\nThis vulnerability is due to improper handling of an endian conversion operation, which may result in an out-of-bounds buffer write. An attacker could exploit this vulnerability by submitting a crafted GPT file to be scanned by ClamAV on an affected device. A successful exploit could allow the attacker to cause the ClamAV scanning process to terminate, resulting in a DoS condition on the affected software.",
